.TH "SOPLOS-APPIMAGE-MANAGER" "1" "2026-11-17" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-appimage-manager \- AppImage manager and desktop integrator for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-appimage-manager
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-appimage-manager
integrates standalone AppImage applications into the desktop.
Built with Tauri 2, Rust, and Svelte, it moves AppImages into
.IR ~/AppImages/ ,
extracts their icon and metadata, creates a menu entry for them, and checks
for updates:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B Integration:
add an AppImage from a file dialog or by dragging it onto the window, and
choose whether to move the file or keep a copy.
.IP \[bu]
.B Metadata extraction:
icon, version, category and comment are read from the AppImage. 7-Zip is used
when available, and the AppImage's own
.B \-\-appimage-extract
is used as a fallback, with an execution timeout.
.IP \[bu]
.B Duplicate detection:
an AppImage with the same name and size as one already integrated is not added twice.
.IP \[bu]
.B Customization:
edit the name, version, description, categories, update endpoint and the optional
"Run as root" launch flag of any AppImage at any time.
.IP \[bu]
.B Updates:
check GitHub releases, GitLab releases, Codeberg or a custom HTTP URL, for a
single application or for all of them.
.IP \[bu]
.B Management:
launch, re-integrate, update, or completely uninstall an AppImage together
with its desktop entry and cached icon.
.IP \[bu]
.B Live monitoring:
changes made inside
.I ~/AppImages/
are detected by a filesystem watcher and shown without restarting.
.P
Everything is done under the user's home directory. The only privileged action
is the per-AppImage "Run as root" option, which launches that AppImage through
.BR pkexec (1).
Launched AppImages run detached from the manager, in their own process group.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Add a new AppImage.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/AppImages/
Storage directory for the integrated AppImages.
.TP
.I ~/AppImages/.icons/
Icons extracted from the integrated AppImages.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/
Desktop entries created for the integrated AppImages.
